        "declaration": "Matrix.finKronecker_selectedBellProjection_bellPinPrevector",
        "name_status": "declared"
      },
      "paper_sources": [
        {
          "version": "September 24, 2026",
          "path": "preprints/A-two-dimensional-area-law-from-a-global-spectral-gap-September-24-2026/build/sections/07-comparators.tex",
          "labels": [
            "comparator:bell-pin"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "license": "Apache-2.0",
      "notices": [],
      "changes": [
        "Independently derive finite-copy Bell contraction from the actual one-copy vectors and spectral selection. Literal products use existing finKronecker; positive actual selected mass is the only normalization or pin premise, and the original vector need not be normalized. Prove the repeated Bell norm, orthogonal projection and simultaneous-copy invariance. Canonical arrow-product coordinates derive factoring of an arbitrary disjoint auxiliary operator without assuming commutation. Schur labels, metric commutation and the subsequent norm estimate are outside these statements."
      ],
      "no_upstream_proof_text_reused": true,
      "verification": {
        "result": "passed",
        "repository": "LionSR/QICLean",
        "revision": "502d0f43d6e86d9f68692a74f92a6c2b1f427ec6",
        "commands": [
